        isFormal: 1
      - id: B
        title: Informal Scroll
        content: "Premises: P and P \u2192 Q. Conclusion: Q.\n\nWe know P is true.
          We are also given that P implies Q. Therefore, Q must be true."
        isFormal: 0
      steps: []
      acceptableOrders: []
      ruleOptions: []
      expectedRule: 
    - kind: 0
      title: Identify Proof Styles
      instructions: Read both proofs and place each on the correct altar.
      context: 
      scrolls:
      - id: A
        title: Even Sum
        content: Two even numbers are made of whole pairs. Putting the pairs together
          leaves no unpaired item, so their sum is even.
        isFormal: 0
      - id: B
        title: Even Sum
        content: 'Claim: Two even integers have an even sum.

          1. Let a
          = 2m and b = 2n. (Definition of even.)

          2. a + b = 2(m + n).
          (Algebra.)

          3. m + n is an integer, so a + b is even. (Definition
          of even.)'
        isFormal: 1
      steps: []
      acceptableOrders: []
      ruleOptions: []
      expectedRule: 
    - kind: 0
      title: Identify Proof Styles
      instructions: Read both proofs and place each on the correct altar.
      context: 
      scrolls:
      - id: A
        title: Odd Sum
        content: 'Claim: Two odd integers have an even sum.

          1. Let a =
          2m + 1 and b = 2n + 1. (Definition of odd.)

          2. a + b = 2(m +
          n + 1). (Algebra.)

          3. m + n + 1 is an integer, so a + b is even.
          (Definition of even.)'
        isFormal: 1
      - id: B
        title: Odd Sum
        content: Each odd number has one leftover after forming pairs. The two leftovers
          form another pair, so the sum is even.
        isFormal: 0
      steps: []
      acceptableOrders: []
      ruleOptions: []
      expectedRule: 
    - kind: 0
      title: Identify Proof Styles
      instructions: Read both proofs and place each on the correct altar.
      context: 
      scrolls:
      - id: A
        title: Even Square
        content: An even number is built from pairs. Squaring it still produces a
          number of complete pairs, so its square is even.
        isFormal: 0
      - id: B
        title: Even Square
        content: "Claim: The square of an even integer is even.\n1. Let n = 2k. (Definition
          of even.)\n2. n\xB2 = 4k\xB2 = 2(2k\xB2). (Algebra.)\n3. 2k\xB2 is an integer,
          so n\xB2 is even. (Definition of even.)"
        isFormal: 1
      steps: []
      acceptableOrders: []
      ruleOptions: []
      expectedRule: 
    - kind: 0
      title: Identify Proof Styles
      instructions: Read both proofs and place each on the correct altar.
      context: 
      scrolls:
      - id: A
        title: Odd Square
        content: "Claim: The square of an odd integer is odd.\n1. Let n = 2k + 1.
          (Definition of odd.)\n2. n\xB2 = 2(2k\xB2 + 2k) + 1. (Algebra.)\n3. 2k\xB2
          + 2k is an integer, so n\xB2 is odd. (Definition of odd.)"
        isFormal: 1
      - id: B
        title: Odd Square
        content: An odd number has a leftover after pairing. When it is squared,
          one leftover remains, so the square is odd.
        isFormal: 0
      steps: []
      acceptableOrders: []
      ruleOptions: []
      expectedRule: 
    - kind: 0
      title: Identify Proof Styles
      instructions: Read both proofs and place each on the correct altar.
      context: 
      scrolls:
      - id: A
        title: Even Plus Odd
        content: The even group has no leftover and the odd group has one. Together
          they still have one leftover, so the sum is odd.
        isFormal: 0
      - id: B
        title: Even Plus Odd
        content: 'Claim: An even integer plus an odd integer is odd.

          1.
          Let a = 2m and b = 2n + 1. (Parity definitions.)

          2. a + b =
          2(m + n) + 1. (Algebra.)

          3. m + n is an integer, so a + b is
          odd. (Definition of odd.)'
        isFormal: 1
      steps: []
      acceptableOrders: []
      ruleOptions: []
      expectedRule: 
    - kind: 0
      title: Identify Proof Styles
      instructions: Read both proofs and place each on the correct altar.
      context: 
      scrolls:
      - id: A
        title: Even Product
        content: 'Claim: An even integer times an integer is even.

          1.
          Let a = 2m and let b be an integer. (Definition of even.)

          2.
          ab = 2(mb). (Algebra.)

          3. mb is an integer, so ab is even. (Definition
          of even.)'
        isFormal: 1
      - id: B
        title: Even Product
        content: An even amount consists of pairs. Taking any whole number of copies
          preserves those pairs, so the product is even.
        isFormal: 0
      steps: []
      acceptableOrders: []
      ruleOptions: []
      expectedRule: 
    - kind: 0
      title: Identify Proof Styles
      instructions: Read both proofs and place each on the correct altar.
      context: 
      scrolls:
      - id: A
        title: Multiples of Three
        content: Each number is made of complete groups of three. Combining the groups
          still gives complete groups of three.
        isFormal: 0
      - id: B
        title: Multiples of Three
        content: 'Claim: The sum of two multiples of 3 is a multiple of 3.

          1.
          Let a = 3m and b = 3n. (Definition of multiple.)

          2. a + b =
          3(m + n). (Algebra.)

          3. m + n is an integer, so 3 divides a
          + b. (Definition of divides.)'
        isFormal: 1
      steps: []
      acceptableOrders: []
      ruleOptions: []
      expectedRule: 
    - kind: 0
      title: Identify Proof Styles
      instructions: Read both proofs and place each on the correct altar.
      context: 
      scrolls:
      - id: A
        title: Even Difference
        content: 'Claim: The difference of two even integers is even.

          1.
          Let a = 2m and b = 2n. (Definition of even.)

          2. a - b = 2(m
          - n). (Algebra.)

          3. m - n is an integer, so a - b is even. (Definition
          of even.)'
        isFormal: 1
      - id: B
        title: Even Difference
        content: Subtracting complete pairs from complete pairs leaves a whole number
          of pairs, so the difference is even.
        isFormal: 0
      steps: []
      acceptableOrders: []
      ruleOptions: []
      expectedRule: 
    - kind: 0
      title: Identify Proof Styles
      instructions: Read both proofs and place each on the correct altar.
