          (Definition of odd.)\n2. n\xB2 = 2(2k\xB2 + 2k) + 1. (Algebra.)\n3. 2k\xB2
          + 2k is an integer, so n\xB2 is odd. (Definition of odd.)"
        isFormal: 1
      - id: C
        title: Odd Successor
        content: An odd number has one item left after pairing. Add one more item
          and it completes a pair, making the successor even.
        isFormal: 0
      - id: D
        title: Odd Successor
        content: 'Claim: The successor of an odd integer is even.

          1. Let
          n = 2k + 1. (Definition of odd.)

          2. n + 1 = 2(k + 1). (Algebra.)

          3.
          k + 1 is an integer, so n + 1 is even. (Definition of even.)'
        isFormal: 1
      steps: []
      acceptableOrders: []
      ruleOptions: []
      expectedRule: 
